# Cases that must be present and `pass` in the result files of the M5 gate
# (scripts/ci-local.sh --verify-result ... --require-env host,A,B --milestone M5; TEST_STRATEGY.md section 10).
# One case id per line; # starts a comment. A skip, an absent case or a failure rejects the gate.
# The ids are the plain criterion ids. A builder writes a plain id only for a run at the criterion parameters
# (6 h soak, 30 min / 16 writers parallel, 50 leak iterations, 20 kill repetitions, disconnect --full, the 8 CPU-hour
# fuzz campaign, each with its negative control); every other run writes the id with the suffix -SHORT (M5-F04).
# The criterion runs reach tests/results/ with `report.py adopt` (M5-F05); ci-local.sh accepts such a file.
# It does not cover the performance criterion 5.6 (the P-* cases, tests/perf).
# Every id here must be one that a real result builder writes as `pass`
# (tests/unit/ci/gate_cases_check.py checks this; S-*-RUN cases exist only on failure and are not listed).

# soak and its negative control
S-SOAK-01
S-SOAK-01-CONTROL

# parallel access
S-PAR-01
S-PAR-01-CONTROL

# leaks
S-LEAK-01
S-LEAK-01-CONTROL

# low disk space and its negative controls
S-NOSPC-01
S-NOSPC-02

# kills: worker, daemon, macFUSE module process, force-detach, controls, the run
S-KILL-01
S-KILL-02
S-KILL-03
S-KILL-04
S-KILL-05
S-KILL-RUN

# disconnect (yank) workloads and their controls
S-DISC-01
S-DISC-02
S-DISC-03
S-DISC-04
S-DISC-05

# fuzz campaign (T-M5-09): 8 CPU-hours, every crash classified (tests/fuzz/campaign/campaign_result.py, adopted with --env A)
F-CAMPAIGN-01
